00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:15,400
is the same as the
solution to the subset,

249
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:18,720
meaning here in this tree,
this four lines of code

250
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:22,290
is the exact same no matter
if the superset of the tree

251
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:25,290
is 1 million nodes
or if it's 1 node.

252
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:26,730
It works for any size tree.

253
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:30,130
And that includes
subtrees inside a tree.

254
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:33,630
As I go up and down the tree
and go through subtrees,

255
00:10:33,630 --> 00:10:34,990
it's the same exact logic.

256
00:10:34,990 --> 00:10:36,990
So that's another reason
recursive solutions are

257
00:10:36,990 --> 00:10:39,660
very popular with trees is
because once you solve it

258
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:43,420
for one node, you don't have
to touch the code again.

259
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,150
OK.

260
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:48,940
Then on line 60, I
find max recursive

261
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,860
is the same exact thing, except
I just check on the right.

262
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,203
If my node right is
not none, then I'm

