309
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,780
But just keep in mind, the
first time I call find key,

310
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:50,830
it's going to take
the root of the tree.

311
00:12:50,830 --> 00:12:53,910
But then as it recurses
down, root.key key each time

312
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,600
is just going to be
the node you're at.

313
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,580
Think of it like the
root of the subtree.

314
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,560
And if you're
thinking, well, that's

315
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,950
confusing, why don't you
just call it the node?

316
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:01,110
Yeah, I agree with you.

317
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:04,530
But root, just as you go down
and down and down looking

318
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:09,015
for that key, that's
what root is, OK.

319
00:13:09,015 --> 00:13:13,740
And then delete node, the
code gets a little bit longer,

320
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:17,440
but it's really the
exact same as a find.

321
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:20,802
It just recurses down
until it finds it.

322
00:13:20,802 --> 00:13:22,260
And then again,
the only difference

323
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:27,370
here is it needs to replace
